\section{Changing which regions are in it}{

\code{atlas_region_remove()} and \code{atlas_region_keep()} drop or select regions by
regex. \code{atlas_region_rename()} rewrites display names without touching
labels. \code{atlas_region_contextual()} keeps a region's geometry as a grey
outline but takes it out of the palette, which is how the brain silhouette
behind an atlas is made; \code{atlas_context_remove()} drops it again.
\code{atlas_region_op()} does boolean geometry between two labels, selected with
\code{regions()} and \code{context()}. \code{atlas_structure_reorder()} changes the order
structures draw in, and \code{atlas_core_add()} joins extra columns onto \verb{$core}.
}

\section{Changing which views are in it}{

\code{atlas_view_keep()}, \code{atlas_view_remove()}, \code{atlas_view_select()} and
\code{atlas_view_reorder()} select and order the 2D views.
\code{atlas_view_remove_region()} drops one region from some views only,
\code{atlas_view_remove_small()} drops slivers below an area, and
\code{atlas_view_gather()} closes the gaps between panels.
}

